<!--
  Backlog body template (Eta). Body-only — frontmatter is synthesized
  from the entity's Zod schema by the authoring pipeline (lib/model/authoring.ts),
  which strips this comment from rendered instances.

  A backlog is a freeform dump for ideas, half-formed tasks, and things
  to triage later. Two usage patterns coexist:

    (a) Multi-item dump: one file holds many ideas; `status:` is never
        set; you delete or strike through promoted items inside the body.

    (b) Single candidate: the whole file represents one idea. When
        promoted, the file gets `status: promoted/task` (or
        `promoted/milestone`) and `result:` pointing at the new
        artifact. The file becomes an archive pointer; the body stays
        as the origin story.

  Field semantics live in the Zod schema (schema.ts) — the frontmatter contract.
-->

# <%= it.title ?? "<Backlog name>" %>

<Dump whatever — ideas, half-formed tasks, things you want to remember
but aren't worth a real task yet. Promote items to real tasks via
`/sdlc:backlog-triage` or `/sdlc:task-new` when they firm up; delete or
strike-through them here once they've moved on. For single-candidate
files, the whole body is the origin story for the idea.>
